		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Questions about setAngularVelocity]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=41713#p41713"><![CDATA[
I recently replied to a similar question and supplied <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?f=9&amp;t=12545#p41711" class="postlink">one way to do it</a>.  Maybe it will work for you.<br><br>The short overview:<br><br>Pick a timeScale &gt; substep timeStep<br>Compute the rotation you need: angle and axis.<br>if angle &lt; someSmallThreshold: angularVelocity = &lt;0,0,0&gt;<br>else: angularVelocity = (angle * timeStep / timeScale) * axis<br><br>Note: slamming the velocity will override effects of external collisions.  If that is what you want: great.  Otherwise you need to be trickier, maybe apply impulses.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=11033">drleviathan</a> — Sun Dec 23, 2018 3:33 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
